# nishu.dev Project Context (LLM Token-Optimized)
# Format: Compact YAML-like DSL | Version: 2.1.0 | Updated: 2026-08-31

PROJECT:
  name: nishu.dev
  type: Next.js 14 Portfolio Web App (App Router, JS/TS hybrid)
  owner: Nishan Rajak (Backend-Focused Software Engineering Student @ ICFAI Univ Jharkhand)
  repo: nishuR31/nishu.dev
  live_url: https://nishudevportfolio.vercel.app
  api_default: https://nishu-dev-api.onrender.com
  branch_active: test-branch (deployed to Vercel; push test-branch:main to promote to prod)

TECH_STACK:
  framework: Next.js 14.2.15 (App Router, Static Site Generation + SSR)
  react: 18.3.1
  typescript: 5.6.2 (in dependencies — NOT devDependencies, required for Vercel build)
  state: Redux Toolkit 2.12.0 + react-redux 9.3.0 (ONLY used for Theme now)
  styling: TailwindCSS 3.4.14 + styled-components 6.5.1 + tailwindcss-animate
  fonts: GeistVF (local), Outfit (Google Fonts)
  image_format: AVIF (logo.avif, logo-84.avif, logo-180.avif, iitSitting.avif, projects/*.avif)
  package_manager: bun (authoritative bun.lock; package-lock.json removed)
  build_cmd: "bun run build" (runs: rm -rf .next && next build)

ENV_VARS:
  NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL: Backend API root (optional; default: https://nishu-dev-api.onrender.com)
  NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND: Alias for API URL (optional fallback)
  NEXT_PUBLIC_FRONTEND_URL: Site canonical root (default: https://nishudevportfolio.vercel.app)
  NEXT_PUBLIC_SERVICE_ID: EmailJS service key
  NEXT_PUBLIC_TEMPLATE_ID: EmailJS template key
  NEXT_PUBLIC_PUBLIC_KEY: EmailJS public key

ROUTING_STRUCTURE:
  app/layout.js: Root layout — No longer fetches portfolio data; renders static shell and Redux Provider for Theme.
  app/(home)/page.jsx: Home (/) — SSR getPortfolioData() → props passed to Hero, About, Experience, GithubProjects, Skills, Certificates, Assistant sections.
  app/experience/page.tsx: /experience — SSR timeline + full write-up via getPortfolioData().
  app/(projects)/projects/page.tsx: /projects — SSR getPortfolioData().
  app/(projects)/projects/[slug]/page.tsx: /projects/[slug] — SSR initial project via getPortfolioData().
  app/(certificates)/certificates/page.tsx: /certificates — SSR getPortfolioData().
  app/contact/page.tsx: /contact — SSR getPortfolioData().
  app/settings/page.tsx: /settings — Theme settings.
  app/not-found.tsx: 404 handler
  app/error.tsx: Runtime error boundary

STATE_MANAGEMENT:
  store/configStore.ts: Redux store setup (themeSlice only, portfolioSlice effectively deprecated/removed).
  store/index.ts: Custom hooks — useTheme. (usePortfolio is fully removed).
  slices/themeSlice.ts: "dark" | "light" | "system" theme.

DATA_SEEDING_FLOW:
  1. Next.js Server Components call `getPortfolioData()` via `lib/portfolio.ts`.
  2. Data is cached automatically by Next.js data cache mechanism.
  3. Parent pages pass data down as props (`portfolioData` or explicit fields) to child feature components.
  4. Explicit error handling via `result.ok` check. If API fails, UI degrades gracefully or shows inline error.
  5. Redux is completely bypassed for portfolio data, eliminating hydration conflicts.

API_DATA_SCHEMA (nishu-dev-api.onrender.com/portfolio → { success, data: {...} }):
  developer: { name, shortName, role, tagline, bio, location, email, about[] }
  featuredProjects: string[]
  social: { email, github, discord, linkedin, leetcode, hackerone, twitter }
  NAV_ITEMS: { href, label }[]
  recentTracks: boolean
  projects[12]: { id, title, description, image, technologies[], github, demo, problem, solution, role, timeline, highlights[], categories[] }
  skills[4]: { title, iconKey, description, bgClass, iconClass, skills: { name, level, hot? }[] }
  experiences[2]: { position, company, period, location, description, responsibilities[], technologies[] }
  contactInfo[]: { iconKey, label, value, link }
  certificates[30]: { url, category, type }
  additionalProjects: string[]
  strengths: string[]
  maintenanceMode: boolean
  siteName: string

KEY_COMPONENTS:
  components/reduxProvider.jsx: Minimal Provider wrapper for Theme state.
  components/features/home/*: All sections refactored to accept portfolioData as props instead of Redux.
  components/layout/Header/index.tsx: Static nav items and theme toggle, no Redux dependencies.
  components/layout/Footer/index.jsx: Static fallback strings, removed Redux.
  components/ui/skeletons.jsx: Fallback loaders.
  lib/portfolio.ts: Server-side getPortfolioData() — Configured with fast retries (5-8s timeout, 1 retry) and returns a typed discriminated union (`{ok, data} | {ok, error}`).

VERCEL_DEPLOYMENT:
  vercel.json: { framework: nextjs, buildCommand: "bun run build", installCommand: "rm -rf node_modules && bun install", outputDirectory: ".next" }
  KNOWN_ISSUE: Vercel build cache can corrupt node_modules; vercel.json installCommand forces wipe
  KNOWN_ISSUE: Render free tier cold-starts (30-50s); lib/portfolio.ts uses 8s timeout with 1 retry max.
  ACTIVE_BRANCH: test-branch → push to main to trigger production build

SEO_AND_INDEXING_ARCHITECTURE:
  robots:
    handler: app/robots.ts (Next.js MetadataRoute.Robots)
    rules: { userAgent: "*", allow: "/" }
    sitemap: "https://nishudevportfolio.vercel.app/sitemap.xml"
  sitemap:
    handler: app/sitemap.ts (Next.js MetadataRoute.Sitemap)
    indexable_pages: ["/", "/projects", "/experience", "/certificates", "/projects/[slug]"]
    excluded_pages: ["/settings", "/socials", "/techstack", "/contact", "/hire"]
  noindex_directives:
    /settings: app/settings/layout.tsx ({ index: false, follow: true })
    /socials: app/socials/page.tsx ({ index: false, follow: true })
    /techstack: app/techstack/page.tsx ({ index: false, follow: true })
  indexable_directives:
    /contact: app/contact/page.tsx ({ index: true, follow: true })
    /hire: app/hire/page.tsx ({ index: true, follow: true })
    /projects: app/projects/page.tsx ({ index: true, follow: true })
    /projects/[slug]: app/projects/[slug]/page.tsx ({ index: true, follow: true })
    /experience: app/experience/page.tsx ({ index: true, follow: true })
    /certificates: app/certificates/page.tsx ({ index: true, follow: true })
  structured_data:
    schemas: ["ProfilePage", "Person", "WebSite", "CollectionPage"]
    entity_id: "https://nishudevportfolio.vercel.app/#person"
    sameAs: [GitHub, LinkedIn, LeetCode, X/Twitter, HackerOne]
  legacy_cleanup:
    removed: [public/robots.txt, public/sitemap.xml, app/(home)/head.js, app/(projects)/projects/head.js]

BUILD_STATS:
  Stage 1 (Rendering & Hydration Fixes): Completed. All components decouple from Redux `usePortfolio`.
  Stage 2 (Architectural Optimization): Completed. GitHub project fetching is decoupled from the homepage via Suspense boundary to prevent blocking.
  Stage 3 (Data Fetching Resilience): Fixed Next.js `Unexpected end of JSON input` bug by removing incompatible `@fastify/compress` from the backend (Bun zlib streaming bug). Data is successfully fetched and rendered.
  Stage 4 (SEO & Google Identity Architecture): Completed. Migrated to App Router robots.ts & sitemap.ts, added noindex directives to utility routes, consolidated metadata API, strengthened Person & ProfilePage JSON-LD schemas.
  Stage 5 (Interactive Visuals): Implemented Option A dual-layer ASCII-to-Photo hover reveal effect for about-photo using public/nishur31.svg and /iitSitting.avif.
  Stage 6 (Performance, TBT & Accessibility Hardening): Replaced Header scroll forced reflows with IntersectionObserver, deferred assistant chat drawer to dynamic non-SSR import, throttled ThemeController DOM mutations, resized oversized media assets (portrait and project screenshots), and added comprehensive accessible names (aria-label) and button types across all interactive controls.
  Build completes successfully.
